<title>SOUTH KOREA: Ssangyong to buy back one million shrs.</title>
<headline>Ssangyong to buy back one million shrs.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Ssangyong Oil Refining Co Ltd said on Wednesday it would buy back one million common shares of its own stock on the open market between March 31 and June 30 to boost its stock price.  </p>
<p>The buyback, representing 1.76 percent of its share capital, will be handled through Ssangyong Investment Securities, a company statement said.</p>
<p>Ssangyong currently holds none of its common shares.</p>
<p>The statement said buy orders would be placed at any time during the period, based on the previous day's closing price.</p>
<p>Ssangyong shares closed at 15,100 won on Wednesday, up 1,100.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5643</p>
</text>
